text:
maya: Quick heads-up: sample app user reported confusing error blob on auth failures. SDKs return different shapes across languages — we need a quick harmonization plan. TL;DR: typed AuthError, RetriableError with retry_hint, and clear 4xx mapping.
sam: u mean like AuthError vs 401-detail? can u paste example
maya: Yes. From iOS sample app: {"error":"Unauthorized","detail":{"code":401,"msg":"token expired"}} but js sdk returns HTTPError{status:401, body:'Unauthorized'} — hard to program defensively
jordan: big :+1: . Also saw 429s with no Retry-After header from Dedicated edge. Devs get 429 but no guidance.
liam: Proposal: SDKs should surface two typed exceptions: AuthError (401/403), RateLimitError (429 + retry_after), and ServiceError for 5xx. Include `retry_after_seconds` optional field.
maya: also add small UX: `human_message` (short user-facing), `internal_code` (stable string) and link to docs url.
sam: can we avoid breaking changes? maybe add as new fields on existing error objects and deprecate later.
jordan: I'll draft a minimal change: -> js: attach `code` & `retry_after` to Error; py: subclasses AuthError/RateLimitError. Backwards compat by keeping message and http_status.
liam: ops-bot: please note that we'll need server to include Retry-After when returning 429s. ops-bot: scheduled follow-up? Also add telemetry event `error_shim_applied`.
ops-bot: Filed infra ticket INF-512 with priority P2 for adding Retry-After header on 429 responses.
maya: perfect. Sam can you add sample snippets to onboarding sample app showing try/catch and fallback auth refresh?
sam: on it. I'll open a PR with js/py snippets and changelog entry. plan: feature-flag the structured fields for 2 weeks.
jordan: should we add e2e test in sampleapp to assert typed exceptions? yes.
liam: I can own server side headers change. I'll sync w/ infra.
maya: ok owners: sam (sdk changes + sampleapp), liam (server headers), jordan (tests + docs). I'll run canary rollout and watch telemetry.
sam: here's a quick doc snippet to copy into onboarding (feel free to shorten):
```js
try {
  await client.generate(...);
} catch (err) {
  if (err.code === 'auth_error' || err instanceof AuthError) {
    await refreshToken();
    // retry once
  } else if (err instanceof RateLimitError || err.retry_after_seconds) {
    // backoff according to err.retry_after_seconds or exponential backoff
  } else {
    throw err;
  }
}
```
sam: I'll include similar python example with `except AuthError` + helper.
jordan: add a tiny doc page mapping http -> typed error, e.g. 401/403 -> AuthError, 429 -> RateLimitError with optional `retry_after_seconds`, 5xx -> ServiceError.
maya: sounds good. We should also emit a telemetry flag when legacy shapes are seen so we can measure adoption. devex-bot: can you add a dashboard?
devex-bot: Created dashboard card "error_shape_adoption" and added a watcher for new legacy-shape spikes.
liam: timeline: PRs by end of week, server header change + infra rollout early next week, feature-flag on for 2w, canary monitor.
maya: thanks all. tiny follow-up: keep messages user-friendly — avoid dumping full stack traces into sampleapp logs. sampleapp should log `human_message` + correlation id only.
sam: noted. PR will include that logging pattern. :rocket:
